1
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:30,960
Lightly leaping over these restless times,

2
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,420
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero.

3
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,480
I wanna dive into paradise

4
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:45,080
so we keep wearing nothing
but the latest trends,

5
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,220
because our natural faces look even better.

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,960
Let it ring

7
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do it.
The dream that started running never stops.

8
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,580
Let's set sail for adventure tomorrow too,
love war.

9
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:10,820
Everybody can do it. Even if we stick out a little,
it doesn't hurt.

10
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:17,860
Holding a restless curiosity,
I was reaching strong and high.

11
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,680
Japan's most irresponsible parent-child duo.

12
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:38,360
Thanks for your hard work.

13
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:43,720
It's cold, isn't it?

14
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,840
With it this cold,
I don't want to go on patrol.

15
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:49,520
Ryotsu, you're saying that again.

16
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,880
A postcard came for you, Ryo-chan.

17
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,760
It's probably mail-order junk anyway.
Just throw it away.

18
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,160
I don't think it's mail-order.

19
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,980
Well, the sender is...

20
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,100
Ryotsu, it's from Yone-san.

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,720
Ryo-san,
isn't it from Yone-san and Fukuro-san?

22
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:08,400
Yeah, well.

23
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:17,000
Ryo-chan, what do you think you're doing?

24
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,300
That's even worse than
a mail-order postcard.

25
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,920
I'm off to patrol.

26
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:30,060
Dear Kankichi,

27
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:31,960
Mom is doing well.

28
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,580
No matter how many postcards I send,
you never write back.

29
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,440
They say no news is good news,

30
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,920
but going years without
a word is just too sad.

31
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:45,420
Dad threw out his back
at the end of last year,

32
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:47,060
and he's become so weak
and frail since then.

33
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,180
Lately,
some days he just stays in bed all day.

34
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:55,660
Kankichi, stop being so stubborn
and just show your face to us once.

35
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:58,760
I'm sure that would help Dad get better.

36
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,420
Please, for goodness' sake, come home.

37
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:05,820
Take care in the cold and don't catch a cold.
From Mom.

38
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,920
Ryo-chan, wait!

39
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:10,680
What?

40
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,340
Why won't you go back home and see them?

41
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:16,680
Shut up! I hate tsukudani and lectures!

42
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:17,720
See ya!

43
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,200
Ryo-chan!

44
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,380
You'd better not.

45
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:25,200
Ryo-san gets really moody
whenever family comes up.

46
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:29,480
Come to think of it, you've never once
talked about your family, have you, senpai?

47
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:31,820
There's a reason he can't talk about it.

48
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:33,260
Chief.

49
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:38,980
Chief, what's the reason
Ryo-chan can't talk about it?

50
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:43,100
I don't know the details either, but

51
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,940
apparently, when he was 18,

52
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:47,880
he had a huge fight with his father and ran away from home.
Ever since,

53
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,660
he apparently hasn't gone back even once.

54
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:53,700
So he really hasn't been home in years,
just like the postcard says?

55
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:58,440
Yeah. Back when I was young, I told him to
stop being so stubbornly proud and go home,

56
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,660
and I urged him to go back to Shibamata.

57
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,740
But it was no use.

58
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:05,700
He said it was because Tora-san had a pretty younger sister,
or something.

59
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,960
Making up excuses like that.

60
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:10,620
Come to think of it,
you said he hates tsukudani and lectures.

61
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:12,640
Every year,
for the summer and year-end gifts,

62
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:15,920
a huge amount of tsukudani gets
sent from his family to the station.

63
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,520
"Thank you for looking after Kankichi."

64
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,440
It comes with a letter asking
us to keep looking after him.

65
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:24,580
He has such a wonderful family,
yet Ryo-chan...

66
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,860
Yeah, why don't we get
Ryo-chan and his dad to make up?

67
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:31,200
Hey, great idea, right?

68
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,040
Wait, what?

69
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:37,140
Then your mom wouldn't have to
write postcards like this anymore.

70
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,760
Don't, don't.

71
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:41,960
Get involved in Ryo's business
and you'll only end up in trouble.

72
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:44,780
Damn it!

73
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,860
Somebody's talking about me

74
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,820
What are you doing, Ō-chan?

75
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:51,300
My back's feeling better today, so...

76
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,920
I was thinking I'd go pray at Sensō-ji,
you know.

77
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:55,680
Hold on a sec.

78
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:59,400
You don't need a racing
paper to go pray, do you?

79
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,000
This is, well

80
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,460
You can't just lie around all
day or you'll go senile, right?

81
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,420
It's like a workout for the brain, see.

82
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:06,100
Well then.

83
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,740
Dad!

84
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,460
Honestly, on the cover where you were
overjoyed after hitting a huge long-shot bet...

85
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,180
even though you threw out your back!

86
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,740
Senpai, please wake up for a moment.

87
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:25,800
I've got something I want to show you. What is it? It's just a navigation system,
isn't it?

88
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:33,480
This one's different from any ordinary navigation system.
It's a super navigation system made by a company in our group.

89
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:43,860
Of course it has traffic information, and every single house and building all over Japan is loaded in,
plus even date spots and hidden food gems.

90
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:46,520
Wow, it even shows maps this detailed?

91
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:50,580
Then let's set a destination
and start the navigation.

92
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:52,700
Is there anywhere you'd like to go?

93
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,440
Hey, I haven't been to Asakusa
even once since coming to Tokyo.

94
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,080
Let's go to Asakusa.

95
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:00,420
Forget that place, pick somewhere else.

96
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:01,100
Why?

97
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:04,660
Well, it's just that,
whatever the reason, skip Asakusa.

98
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:08,520
I see. Asakusa does feel kind of unpolished,
doesn't it?

99
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,320
Right? Asakusa doesn't have any
fun places to hang out, either.

100
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,860
That's so lame.

101
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:19,320
Yeah, there doesn't seem to
be anything worth seeing there.

102
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:21,200
Let's go to Roppongi or Shibuya.

103
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:25,100
Don't mess with me. Asakusa is lame?

104
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,040
Don't talk nonsense.

105
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:27,960
W-what?

106
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,440
Asakusa has been the center of culture since the Edo period,
you know.

107
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:34,380
Compared to Asakusa,
Roppongi and Shibuya are nothing.

108
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:35,680
They're just a bunch of greenhorns.

109
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,920
But Ryo-chan said -

110
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:39,440
Shut up!
Saying there's nothing worth seeing?

111
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,420
Bring it on.

112
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:43,840
I'll show you how
wonderful Asakusa really is.

113
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:54,180
Good morning! Let's start the route guide!

114
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:58,560
Isn't this voice that of popular
anime voice actress Maya Katsuragi?

115
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,640
Ryo-chan, keep Maya company
all the way to Asakusa, okay?

116
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,460
I'll do it, I'll do it!

117
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,100
Oh my, talking to the navigation like that.

118
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:11,220
If you enter a name,
it guides you to talk to that person.

119
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:15,860
By the way, this is the popular voice actress version.
There are lots of other software versions too.

120
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:21,080
Not like that, that's no good!
Slow down more!

121
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,700
What is this software?

122
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,860
Wouldn't a Nakagawa version be better?

123
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,780
It's the adult video actress version,
after all.

124
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,820
Change it to a different one already.

125
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:35,040
Damn, I should have turned
left at that intersection.

126
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,860
Why aren't you turning left, you idiot!
I'll win!

127
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,340
You lousy navigator, you bastard!

128
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:44,240
Ryo-chan, calm down! What are you doing,
going to punch the navigation?!

129
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:48,340
The yakuza version doesn't seem to suit a senior like you very well,
does it?

130
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:08,800
Wow, it's full of tourists, isn't it?

131
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,340
That's a huge lantern.

132
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,940
Ryo-chan, what is this?

133
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:16,320
You don't even know Kaminarimon?

134
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:17,400
Tagumon

135
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,860
They say he had a really fearsome face,
didn't he?

136
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:20,900
What's this?

137
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,620
This is Raijin, the Thunder God.

138
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:25,020
And this one is Fujin, the Wind God.

139
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:29,440
And if you go through this area with the shops,
it leads to Sensō-ji.

140
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:32,820
Even though it's a weekday morning,
it's pretty busy.

141
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:35,240
Compared to the old days,
it's quite a bit less now.

142
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,920
Freshly made ones really are the best

143
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:58,300
Look, it's Ryo-chan, isn't it?

144
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,400
Eating over here too

145
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,360
I'll have this, this, and this too!

146
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,880
It's Ryo-chan, isn't it?

147
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,520
Isn't that Kan-chan?

148
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,060
Auntie, how have you been?

149
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,260
Brings back memories.

150
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:12,040
Hey, Kan-chan's back!

151
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,420
Kankichi! Long time no see.

152
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,680
It's the old man!

153
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,360
Hey, still knocking back the sake as usual?

154
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:19,260
Your missus must be crying her eyes out.

155
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:22,300
Of all people, you actually became a cop

156
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:26,360
I was looking forward to you wrecking this place in three days,
you know.

157
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:27,340
What's that supposed to mean?

158
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,740
You haven't changed a bit.
Still hot-blooded.

159
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,760
And after all these years, too.

160
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:38,040
You're really popular, Senpai. This whole
area is basically your home turf, isn't it?

161
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:02,100
Shall we go to the downtown
Disneyland or something?

162
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,520
Downtown Disneyland.

163
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,520
Aaaaaaah!

164
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:22,480
This roller coaster is packed with thrills.

165
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:25,440
After all, it nearly crashes
right into people's houses!

166
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:28,720
Anyway,
Ryo-chan's family home is near here, right?

167
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,940
I want to see it.

168
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:32,520
Don't be ridiculous!

169
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,120
We're on duty, you know!

170
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:35,160
We're going back.

171
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:39,480
I didn't know
"on duty" was even in Ryo-chan's dictionary.

172
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:43,260
Shut up! I haven't been back in years.
I've even forgotten the way.

173
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:46,340
Then don't worry,
we have the navigation system.

174
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:49,420
Come on, we've come all this way.

175
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:52,560
Coming to Asakusa and not visiting
Sensō-ji is like not visiting at all.

176
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,000
So that's it! You two set me up, didn't you?

177
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,120
Hey, let go!

178
00:10:56,120 --> 00:11:02,880
Wow, so that's Ryo-chan's house?

179
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,540
Well, you've seen it now,
so that's enough, right?

180
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:09,360
What are you talking about? We've come all this way,
so you should at least show your face.

181
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:11,820
Look! Isn't that Ryo-chan's mom?

182
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,300
Yikes!

183
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:19,680
Look, Senpai!

184
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:23,880
Idiot! Ever since that fight with Dad at 18
over whether to take over the family business,

185
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,100
I swore I'd never cross
that threshold again!

186
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:29,200
But I heard your father's
laid up with lumbago.

187
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,000
You should go visit him.

188
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:34,580
I was disowned and cut off!
I can't go back now!

189
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,300
I'm walking home.

190
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,920
Ryo-chan, we've come all this way!

191
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:46,660
Senpai, why don't we grab a bite to eat?
My treat.

192
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:50,300
If you're buying, that changes things.

193
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,400
It's delicious, isn't it?

194
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,580
It's like a chomolog, you know.

195
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,780
And the price is ridiculously cheap, too.

196
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:08,640
Really.

197
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,860
With this taste and portion,
it'd cost more than double in Ginza.

198
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:12,900
How about that, Reiko?

199
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,220
Have you come to appreciate Asakusa now?

200
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:16,300
Yes, yes, I stand corrected.

201
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:18,800
Good, good.

202
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,800
After all, Asakusa is the best.

203
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,340
Asakusa is the best, you know.

204
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,660
Are you an idiot or what?

205
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,060
No way, that's absolutely not it.

206
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,180
If some lame guy like this shows up,
you'll be the one getting shocked, bring it on!

207
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,180
We'll swing the doors wide open,
Kannon-style.

208
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,440
Still, here's the favorite, though.

209
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,140
If it's Tokyo, it's Roppongi, obviously.

210
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,420
Yo-chuu!

211
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:40,280
Hey, you get cocky just because
I kept quiet and listened!

212
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:43,240
Hey, you shitty old geezer,
you're trashing Asakusa to shit!

213
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:46,400
Even if the Kannon goddess forgives you,
I won't!

214
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:50,420
How the hell did you
figure out my horse pick?

215
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,400
You...

216
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:20,980
Ryo-san, wasn't that...

217
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:22,460
Shut up.

218
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:28,260
What's going on? Do you know that guy?

219
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,400
I know him, yeah, but...

220
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:34,320
He called you Ryo-san too, you know.

221
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,640
There are quite a few
people like him around here.

222
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,400
Never mind about that.

223
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,880
Could he be your father?

224
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:40,620
No, he isn't.

225
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,360
Well then, go ahead.

226
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:46,520
So that current person's wife

227
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:49,800
is like the one who gave
birth to me forty years ago.

228
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,140
After all, isn't he your father?

229
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:56,780
Well, that seems to be
how people commonly put it.

230
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,380
Kei-chan, you did it, didn't you?

231
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:01,540
Come on, Ryo-chan, let's say hello.

232
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:03,260
Not now, it's awkward.

233
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,700
Later, later.

234
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:06,540
It's too late to be awkward now.

235
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,620
That's right, senpai.

236
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:10,840
Come on, go on.

237
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,960
Somehow, the next door is noisy.

238
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,980
Senpai went in

239
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,900
It's nice to meet you for the first time.

240
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,860
My name is Keiichi Nakagawa.

241
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:23,280
I'm always indebted to you, senpai.

242
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,360
I'm Reiko Akimoto.

243
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:26,860
Nice to meet you.

244
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:28,820
Well, thank you.

245
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,520
Are you all right?

246
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:34,940
This is nothing, no problem at all.

247
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:40,000
What are you doing?
You're father and son, at least say hello.

248
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:42,120
Ryo-chan.

249
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,220
Senpai.

250
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,220
Fine, I get it.

251
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,560
Hello, how are you.

252
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:51,460
I'm Ryo-chan, your son. Do you remember me?

253
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:57,240
So it's you. I thought I'd seen
that face somewhere earlier.

254
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,440
Don't give me that innocent act,
you bastard.

255
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:03,780
Are they really father and son?

256
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:06,320
I'm starting to doubt it myself.

257
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:09,300
We shouldn't interrupt
their long-awaited reunion.

258
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,260
Yotsu-san, I'll be going now.

259
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,960
Wait, there's more to it.

260
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:20,020
The main race is a sure thing,
with a box bet on Bokujō-ō.

261
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,240
Yes, yes, take your time.

262
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,120
Thank you very much.

263
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,120
Thank you very much.

264
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:24,680
Thank you very much.

265
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:33,740
So "Asakusa Ichiban" was a horse racing tip?
Way to be misleading, you jerk!

266
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,020
Ryo-chan, say something.

267
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,580
You haven't seen each other in ages,
after all.

268
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:54,240
Ma'am, are you still making tsukudani?

269
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,320
We're managing, thanks to you.

270
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,620
Father,
please take the lead and talk to him.

271
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:04,420
He's just embarrassed, Senpai.

272
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:05,880
Is that so?

273
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:09,800
Yes, well, these days police officers
get all sorts of media attention, you know,

274
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:11,951
like being featured and such,

275
00:16:12,001 --> 00:16:14,980
I imagine it must be tough for you too

276
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,860
No, he's pretty much given up on him by now.

277
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,720
It's just like a formal matchmaking meeting,
isn't it.

278
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,180
It doesn't even seem like a
conversation between father and son.

279
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,740
I can't take this atmosphere anymore.

280
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:45,760
Geez.

281
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,620
Dad's skipping out on the shop

282
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:49,800
and making horse race
predictions here of all places,

283
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,440
that's just not right.

284
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:53,980
If you're sick,
you should act like it and stay home.

285
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,040
Seriously!

286
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:58,180
How could I make horse predictions when
I'm scared my lumbago will flare up?

287
00:16:58,940 --> 00:17:00,400
Don't say such ridiculous things.

288
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,600
If Dad had just quietly minded the shop,

289
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,480
we wouldn't have run into each other here.

290
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:05,640
You're one to talk.

291
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,120
It's your fault for coming
to Asakusa of all places.

292
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:10,520
You said you'd never
set foot in Asakusa again,

293
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:11,560
and then stormed off, didn't you?

294
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,500
That idiot Reiko said she wanted to come,
so we ended up here.

295
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,880
I don't know anything about it.

296
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:22,440
Now, now, you two.
You're bothering the other customers here.

297
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,680
Let's move somewhere else.

298
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,580
Excuse me, the bill, please!

299
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,800
Coming!

300
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:34,820
Honestly, what a pair of father and son.
I can't keep up with them.

301
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,120
You can't drink it, the marble gets stuck.

302
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,120
This, this.

303
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:49,460
With ramune, you hold the marble
in place with this bump and drink.

304
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:50,880
Is that so?

305
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,600
Well, that's how it went.

306
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,820
This guy's so stubborn.

307
00:17:56,280 --> 00:18:00,220
Well, looking back,
I think I was childish too.

308
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:03,180
It's Dad's fault for making
me eat nothing but tsukudani.

309
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:06,780
I even got the nickname
"Tsukudani Taro" in elementary school.

310
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:11,000
That was so you'd get nutrition and grow up fast,
you see.

311
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,740
Eating tsukudani every day would actually cause nutritional problems,
you know.

312
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:15,920
Honestly, the only joke here is your face.

313
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:19,860
You look like Gonra, and I don't
want to hear about faces from you.

314
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:23,200
What did you say, you rotten know-it-all!

315
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,960
How dare you talk to your father like that!

316
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,740
Wanna go?

317
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:29,000
Don't get cocky!

318
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:34,580
Ow!

319
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:34,980
Kajira!

320
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,660
Kajira, I'm telling you!

321
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:40,300
Kajira! Kajira!

322
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:41,820
Oradhuidhuida!

323
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,460
Hey, wait up, Dad!

324
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,800
Dukudoku! Kaji is Dad's pride and joy!

325
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:48,620
Dukudoku! Dukudoku!

326
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:53,420
Looks like you two
really are father and son.

327
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,660
Dad, you're judging by appearances too!

328
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,300
Hey, hey, come on, I can't drink that!

329
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,800
Haven't the fire engines arrived yet?

330
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:06,800
This is bad.

331
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:09,580
It looks like that old
lady is still in her room.

332
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:10,800
Hey, where is she?

333
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,680
At the far end of the second floor.

334
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,480
Over there

335
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:15,700
Help!

336
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:20,020
Kankichi, I'll save that hostess girl.

337
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,540
You take care of the old woman.

338
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:24,080
Why do I have to take the old woman?

339
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,440
Wait, Dad!

340
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:26,820
Hey, why me?

341
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,660
Hostess girl!

342
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,880
Why me?

343
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,200
Boy, boy!

344
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:33,460
Granny, are you all right?

345
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:36,280
Please,

346
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:39,260
I sprained my leg,

347
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:41,140
come on, miss.

348
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:41,980
Sorry.

349
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,440
This is unbearable.

350
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:47,060
Alright, let's go, miss.

351
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:48,760
Up we go.

352
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:54,920
Dad, what are you doing? Hurry up!

353
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,100
My lumbago flared up again.

354
00:19:58,580 --> 00:19:59,860
At a time like this!

355
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:02,220
Miss, hold on to my shoulder.

356
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:02,860
Yes.

357
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,640
Dad, I'm coming to save you right away,
so hang on!

358
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:26,420
Please look after these two.

359
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:27,940
Ryo-chan

360
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:28,580
Senpai

361
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:34,020
Senpai, what are you doing?

362
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,620
I don't have time to explain.

363
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,560
This is too dangerous!

364
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,780
Leave this to us!

365
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:39,820
Shut up!

366
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:40,640
Get out of the way!

367
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,140
I told you no!

368
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:42,800
Let go!

369
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:44,240
Dad's climbing up!

370
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:44,700
What!

371
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:47,580
Senpai!

372
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:55,300
Damn it! What is Kankichi doing?

373
00:20:55,300 --> 00:21:20,220
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

374
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:29,880
Yo-chan

375
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,300
Senpai

376
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,140
No way

377
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:45,300
Senpai!

378
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,160
You had us worried sick.

379
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:49,780
Like I'd die from something like this!

380
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:58,820
Ow ow!

381
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:01,400
Reiko-chan, put the patch on more gently.

382
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,340
I'm sorry.

383
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,920
Reiko, don't apologize.

384
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:08,760
This happened because you
got lecherous at your age.

385
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:11,320
Coming from a dirty old pervert like you?

386
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:12,180
What did you say?

387
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:16,920
Reiko-chan, I didn't grow any
hair down there until third grade.

388
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:20,900
Enough already!
Who do you think saved your life?

389
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,880
Who asked you to save me?

390
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:26,160
I could've gotten out on my own,
but you had to butt in.

391
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:28,620
I'm your goddamn father!

392
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,760
What did you say,
you good-for-nothing little shit!

393
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:36,354
Senpai,
this is the part where the article is, but

394
00:22:36,404 --> 00:22:38,260
We should head back soon,
or the Chief will...

395
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,860
Oh right,
we left without telling anyone, didn't we.

396
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:43,640
That's how it is, Dad. Take care.

397
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:49,740
Thank you for the meal.
I had a wonderful time, Uncle.

398
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:51,120
Glad to hear it.

399
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:52,740
Excuse us.

400
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:59,100
Won't you stop by the family home?
Mom's worried about you.

401
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:04,680
No, not today. I'm on duty right now.

402
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:08,100
Officer Ryotsu, returning to duty now.

403
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:11,560
I'll come again, Ryo-san.

404
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:13,580
Yeah, see you.

405
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:20,700
Looks like even that guy is
weak when it comes to his mother

406
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:26,580
At your age, still a patrol officer.
I won't say it's pathetic.

407
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:30,740
That's not true. You've become a fine police officer,
haven't you?

408
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:33,500
In my book, you're still a greenhorn.

409
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:35,940
Hey, San-chan,
go bring another bottle, will you?

410
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:36,520
Yes.

411
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,820
That idiot.

412
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:45,760
Ryo-chan's dad is a fun guy, isn't he?

413
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:46,440
Yeah.

414
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:48,500
He's just like Ryo-chan.

415
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:50,780
Let's come again, senpai.

416
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,620
Maybe once a year, then.

417
00:23:57,220 --> 00:23:58,240
We'll come again...

418
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:07,880
Property damage, violation of the Road Traffic Act,
abuse of authority.

419
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:10,360
Is this how a police officer who's
supposed to protect citizens behaves?

420
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:14,800
Ryotsu Kankichi and Honda Hayato,
you are both banned from the premises.

421
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:18,340
Chief, that wasn't us! We're innocent!

422
00:24:18,340 --> 00:24:22,000
Being banned doesn't scare me.
See you next time.

423
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if we try to stop the clock,

424
00:24:34,820 --> 00:24:37,720
time keeps on passing.

425
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:42,620
Crying with a scowl on our faces,

426
00:24:44,300 --> 00:24:48,080
let's laugh it off and keep on living.

427
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:53,040
Even if today

428
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:57,920
is rainy,

429
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:03,460
tomorrow will be sunny.

430
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,340
Bye-bye.

431
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:13,860
Bye-bye,
let's wave goodbye to the unpleasant things.

432
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:23,940
Oh yeah, let's live as we like,
good things will come.

433
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:30,220
Outside the door,
the stars are calling for you.

434
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:41,320
Thank you for watching.

